Bobony Roleplay - Streamer Conduct Rules

All streamers who broadcast content from Bobony Roleplay must follow these guidelines to ensure a respectful and positive community environment:

Maintain a Positive Image – Streamers are required to uphold the reputation of the server. Speaking negatively about Bobony RP in any way is strictly prohibited.

Follow Server Rules – All streamers must abide by the server’s rules and ensure that their content does not promote or encourage rule-breaking.

💢 Failure to comply may result in penalties, bans or server restrictions. Keep the Bobony RP experience enjoyable for everyone! 🚀

  Bans from 48h to PERMA 

  🚫 Streamer Rule – OOC Insults (Strict)

Streamers are strictly NOT allowed to insult, mock, or verbally attack any player outside of their character while streaming.

❌ Not Allowed

Insulting a player personally (OOC)

Using real-life insults, slurs, or humiliating language

Targeting a player’s voice, accent, appearance, or personal traits

Saying “it’s just jokes” or “stream content” as an excuse




